            {
                "entry_id": "d556f671-8048-388b-87c1-a4b99c457bdc",
                "word": "lexie",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "9885a7d5-ef4c-48a5-91e6-8d2825abfacc",
                        "entry_id": "d556f671-8048-388b-87c1-a4b99c457bdc",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "lexies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a9cf0efd-fb4a-3dc7-8155-ea7ae5b360e6",
                        "entry_id": "d556f671-8048-388b-87c1-a4b99c457bdc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Élément unitaire du lexique, comme un mot simple (lexème), une locution ou un proverbe. Par exemple, jeune, jeune homme et les voyages forment la jeunesse sont des lexies."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "67abd278-7c74-4a1c-87b8-7c5eada34833",
                                "sense_id": "a9cf0efd-fb4a-3dc7-8155-ea7ae5b360e6",
                                "text": "En second lieu, dans les usages qui nous intéressent, le syntagme « petite phrase » apparaît comme une lexie, c’est-à-dire comme une unité formant un tout spécifique, non réductible à l’addition de ses composantes (et non pas comme une expression libre, que l’on pourrait modifier sans grands changements de sens, par exemple en disant « phrase succincte ») […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b39feb00-b3ee-42e3-9810-b6a4e7950212",
                        "source_entry_id": "d556f671-8048-388b-87c1-a4b99c457bdc",
                        "source_sense_id": "a9cf0efd-fb4a-3dc7-8155-ea7ae5b360e6",
                        "source_sense_description": "Élément unitaire du lexique",
                        "target_lang_word": "lexikalische Einheit",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e9ffa3f8-44a0-4720-b2e7-5050137cd3e9",
                        "source_entry_id": "d556f671-8048-388b-87c1-a4b99c457bdc",
                        "source_sense_id": "a9cf0efd-fb4a-3dc7-8155-ea7ae5b360e6",
                        "source_sense_description": "Élément unitaire du lexique",
                        "target_lang_word": "lexical item",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "lexical item",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4514e553-f48f-3bc8-84bf-3fc346c40382",
                                        "entry_id": "de45ac67-0c49-3c26-9276-b180448b5163",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A term (that is, a word or sequence of words) that acts as a unit of meaning, including words, phrases, phrasal verbs and proverbs; exemplified by cat, traffic light, take care of, by-the-way, and don't count your chickens before they hatch."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "41e06004-a361-4969-995e-47e5cded1066",
                                                "sense_id": "4514e553-f48f-3bc8-84bf-3fc346c40382",
                                                "text": "For quotations using this term, see Citations:lexical item."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "71a4de2e-68dc-4719-8080-d30424364766",
                                                "sense_id": "4514e553-f48f-3bc8-84bf-3fc346c40382",
                                                "text": "He also realized that by comparing different types of text you may be able to spot \"a different density ( repetition rate ) of lexical items, and different degrees of cohesion, in the short story and in the novel."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fd6e141c-f6c4-48d1-bcff-bd8b93a7ad1e",
                                                "sense_id": "4514e553-f48f-3bc8-84bf-3fc346c40382",
                                                "text": "It is not surprising that this is a very common structure in language, because it allows the flexibility that was identified earlier in this paper as essential for an adequate lexical item."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9d56738b-5e6c-47f4-92b6-a780dbec2ed7",
                                                "sense_id": "4514e553-f48f-3bc8-84bf-3fc346c40382",
                                                "text": "The meaning of lexical items may be described in terms of combinations of semantic features."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eda40e83-0a25-4e3f-bc9b-ce87aaa40959",
                                                "sense_id": "4514e553-f48f-3bc8-84bf-3fc346c40382",
                                                "text": "Thus there are 3751 lexical items covered in total. Taking into account polysemy, there are 4315 separate senses."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
